From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: nadelacruz-00 <323917690+nadelacruz-00@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 28 Oct 2026 15:20:04 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] Revert "drm/msm/a6xx: erhai: retry+escalate runtime GMU OOB
 timeouts; name UKIs bXX.efi"

This reverts commit cbfce58e8e50 (a6xx_gmu.c hunks only).

The runtime OOB timeouts the original retried and escalated were a symptom
of the mis-sized device tree windows (the RSCC at gpu+0x50000 outside the
GPU node's 0x40000 kgsl_3d0_reg_memory window, and the GX GDSC left unbound
by 9c9eefdef1 because the gxclkctl node mapped only 4 KiB), which left the
GMU unable to be reset; with the windows fixed the upstream
single-handshake OOB path is used again.

postinst left untouched: the original commit also renamed UKIs.

Tested on a OnePlus Pad 3 (SM8750) with the whole series: the GPU
powers up at probe (no -19), the CX GDSC collapses on runtime suspend,
IGT msm_recovery gpu-fault recovers in 5 of 5 runs, and 2.5 h of desktop
use ran 3,227 runtime-PM cycles without a GMU wedge.

Signed-off-by: nadelacruz-00 <323917690+nadelacruz-00@users.noreply.github.com>
---
 drivers/gpu/drm/msm/adreno/a6xx_gmu.c | 71 ++++++---------------------
 1 file changed, 14 insertions(+), 57 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/adreno/a6xx_gmu.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/adreno/a6xx_gmu.c
index 01367c13e78..64e8d1ba8b8 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/adreno/a6xx_gmu.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/adreno/a6xx_gmu.c
@@ -500,7 +500,6 @@ int a6xx_gmu_set_oob(struct a6xx_gmu *gmu, enum a6xx_gmu_oob_state state)
 	int ret;
 	u32 val;
 	int request, ack;
-	int attempt;
 
 	WARN_ON_ONCE(!mutex_is_locked(&gmu->lock));
 
@@ -525,47 +524,26 @@ int a6xx_gmu_set_oob(struct a6xx_gmu *gmu, enum a6xx_gmu_oob_state state)
 		}
 	}
 
-	/*
-	 * erhai: retry the OOB handshake a bounded number of times. The a8xx
-	 * GMU can drop the ack under load / a slow resume; a single 10 ms poll
-	 * then spuriously times out and the caller treats an otherwise fine
-	 * GMU as wedged (feeding the OOB-timeout storm that preceded the
-	 * hangcheck lockups on 2026-09-12). Mirrors the CM3-boot retry in
-	 * a6xx_gmu_start(): a glitchy handshake self-heals instead of wedging.
-	 */
-	for (attempt = 0; attempt < 3; attempt++) {
-		/* Trigger the requested OOB operation */
-		gmu_write(gmu, REG_A6XX_GMU_HOST2GMU_INTR_SET, 1 << request);
-
-		do {
-			/* Wait for the acknowledge interrupt */
-			ret = gmu_poll_timeout(gmu, REG_A6XX_GMU_GMU2HOST_INTR_INFO, val,
-				val & (1 << ack), 100, 10000);
-
-			if (!ret)
-				break;
-
-			if (completion_done(&a6xx_gpu->base.fault_coredump_done))
-				break;
+	/* Trigger the equested OOB operation */
+	gmu_write(gmu, REG_A6XX_GMU_HOST2GMU_INTR_SET, 1 << request);
 
-			/* We may timeout because the GMU is temporarily wedged from
-			 * pending faults from the GPU and we are taking a devcoredump.
-			 * Wait until the MMU is resumed and try again.
-			 */
-			wait_for_completion(&a6xx_gpu->base.fault_coredump_done);
-		} while (true);
+	do {
+		/* Wait for the acknowledge interrupt */
+		ret = gmu_poll_timeout(gmu, REG_A6XX_GMU_GMU2HOST_INTR_INFO, val,
+			val & (1 << ack), 100, 10000);
 
 		if (!ret)
 			break;
 
-		/* Clear the acknowledge interrupt before trying again */
-		gmu_write(gmu, REG_A6XX_GMU_GMU2HOST_INTR_CLR, 1 << ack);
+		if (completion_done(&a6xx_gpu->base.fault_coredump_done))
+			break;
 
-		if (attempt < 2)
-			DRM_DEV_INFO(gmu->dev,
-				"erhai: GMU OOB set %s attempt %d/3 timed out, retrying\n",
-				a6xx_gmu_oob_bits[state].name, attempt + 1);
-	}
+		/* We may timeout because the GMU is temporarily wedged from
+		 * pending faults from the GPU and we are taking a devcoredump.
+		 * Wait until the MMU is resumed and try again.
+		 */
+		wait_for_completion(&a6xx_gpu->base.fault_coredump_done);
+	} while (true);
 
 	if (ret)
 		DRM_DEV_ERROR(gmu->dev,
@@ -576,27 +554,6 @@ int a6xx_gmu_set_oob(struct a6xx_gmu *gmu, enum a6xx_gmu_oob_state state)
 	/* Clear the acknowledge interrupt */
 	gmu_write(gmu, REG_A6XX_GMU_GMU2HOST_INTR_CLR, 1 << ack);
 
-	/*
-	 * erhai: runtime GMU wedge escalation. The observed killer
-	 * (2026-09-12 #86 boot -2 00:02, boot -1 00:04) is the a8xx GMU
-	 * silently refusing to ack OOB at runtime — no WDOG_BITE / CM3_FAULT
-	 * IRQ, just three 10 ms GPU_SET timeouts -> hangcheck "gpu lockup
-	 * rb 0" with uncompleted fences -> recover_worker -> "gpu fault
-	 * iova=0x0" -> frozen display with an otherwise-alive system, because
-	 * the graceful a6xx_gmu_shutdown()'s own OOB retry also times out and
-	 * the CX gdsc never collapses. Escalate immediately instead: mark the
-	 * GMU hung and queue the recover work so the full force_off (CM3
-	 * sysreset + RPMh stop) + cold re-boot path runs instead of the
-	 * graceful-but-wedged one. gmu->hung gates this to one report per
-	 * wedge (recovery clears it on the next resume).
-	 */
-	if (ret && !gmu->hung) {
-		DRM_DEV_INFO(gmu->dev,
-			"erhai: GMU OOB set %s wedged after 3 attempts - escalating to full GPU recovery\n",
-			a6xx_gmu_oob_bits[state].name);
-		a6xx_gmu_fault(gmu);
-	}
-
 	return ret;
 }
 
